Read offline by the build from files, matched by identifiers (round
eighty-seven):

  Predicted extinction risk for all Angiosperm species, v1.0 (2024-02-01).
    Bachman, S.P., Brown, M.J.M., Leão, T.C.C., Nic Lughadha, E., Walker, B.E.
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10605228. CC BY 4.0. Paper: New Phytologist
    242: 797-808, https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.19592. IUCN categories in the
    file are not used.
  CITES Appendices I, II and III (valid from 5 March 2026), CITES Secretariat,
    https://cites.org/eng/app/appendices.php: plant listings transcribed by
    hand (src/lib/dossier/cites-appendices.tsv). No Species+ or CITES
    Checklist data.
  ChromoDB Source Data: Chromosome counts from the IAPT/IOPB chromosome data
    series, v3.1 (2026-11-08). Simon, J., Bosch, M., Blanché, C.
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24057855. CC BY 4.0.
  World Flora Online Plant List, release 2026-06 (2026-06-21).
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20782718. CC0 1.0.

Read, and published only as codes, names or links: the level-3 region codes
and names of TDWG's World Geographical Scheme for Recording Plant
Distributions, 2nd edition, and its tables that place states and provinces in
regions (github.com/tdwg/wgsrpd; TDWG's own boundary polygons are not used);
IPNI and POWO identifiers (RBG Kew), and IPNI's records of names, read to
prove an identifier; iNaturalist taxon identifiers; the page addresses of
the Biodiversity Heritage Library (biodiversitylibrary.org), asked of its
resolver for a name's place of publication and only linked; and the
titles and descriptions of GBIF's datasets, read to tell living collections
from genebanks when the species list was made.

Cited as definitions, not read as data: the zones of the USDA Plant
Hardiness Zone Map (planthardiness.ars.usda.gov), the RHS hardiness rating's
bands (rhs.org.uk), the Köppen-Geiger thresholds of Peel, Finlayson and
McMahon (2007), Hydrology and Earth System Sciences 11: 1633-1644
(https://doi.org/10.5194/hess-11-1633-2007), and the scale of Walter and
Lieth's climate diagrams.

The frost watch, which is no part of the reference, shows forecasts asked for
your site: from MET Norway (api.met.no; CC BY 4.0) and, in the
US and its territories, from the National Weather Service (public domain).

